  "_comment": "Hand-verified labels for outputs/crops/*.jpg, re-verified from scratch after project_bottle_bases() was fixed to capture each bottle's full height (base through neck/cap-thread) instead of just the cylindrical body -- the old crops cut off the neck area entirely, hiding neck deformities and some upper-body defects. Zero-tolerance standard: ANY visible mark, speck, or discoloration on the bottle -- no matter how small -- is labeled defective. A bottle is only clean if its surface is pure, unbroken white with nothing visible on it. Two crops show a foreign object (cloth/packaging fragment) draped over the bottle neck, obscuring it -- these are labeled defective since cleanliness at the neck cannot be confirmed: bottle_0002.jpg, IMG_9792_bottle_0005.jpg. Two crops are unusable and deliberately omitted (not clean or defective, just excluded): bottle_0002... wait see below -- IMG_9791_bottle_0016.jpg (a person's hand fills the frame, no clean bottle view) is omitted. False-tracker-detection crops with no bottle at all are also omitted: IMG_9792_bottle_0024.jpg, IMG_9794_bottle_0020.jpg, IMG_9796_bottle_0023.jpg (these may not exist as files after the detector fix changed capture timing/count; kept out either way). Four crops (IMG_9792_bottle_0006/0015, IMG_9793_bottle_0003, IMG_9796_bottle_0011) were corrected from clean to defective after a live YOLO-threshold experiment at 60% confidence surfaced them as false negatives; a real Claude re-analysis confirmed genuine defects (factory_defect neck deformation / small dirty specks) that the original manual review had missed.",
